<title>SINGAPORE: Pacific Century back in profit in 1996.</title>
<headline>Pacific Century back in profit in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				2.22 vs   14.74 (loss)</p>
<p>Group shr (cents)		     1.45 vs    9.62 (loss)</p>
<p>    Turnover				110.28 vs  115.15</p>
<p>    Investment income		     0.22 vs    0.19</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	97.22 vs   73.59</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    3.34 vs    0.97</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	   5.15 vs    5.43</p>
<p>    Losses from associates		0.11 vs    nil</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  1.62 vs   15.68 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax					 0.32 vs    0.49</p>
<p>    Minorities				0.19 vs    0.45</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			19.19 vs   55.84</p>
<p>Note - Pacific Century Regional Developments Ltd has wide-ranging interests, including insurance, manufacturing, and property.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
